WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.610
Two pizzas sit side by side.

2
00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:07.220
The small one is twenty centimetres
across and costs six pounds.

3
00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:10.110
The large one is forty centimetres across.

4
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:12.370
It costs eighteen pounds.

5
00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:16.430
So it's twice as wide,
but three times the cost.

6
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:17.960
Are you being ripped off?

7
00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:21.010
Or does the big pizza
hold more than it looks?

8
00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:24.740
Good deal, bad deal, or does it even out?

9
00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:28.930
In this mission, you'll find the
best buy by comparing the same unit,

10
00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:30.850
like price per gram.

11
00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:34.600
You'll see that for a pizza, what
you actually get is its area,

12
00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:36.430
not its diameter.

13
00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:40.210
Then you'll work out how much
pizza each pound buys you.

14
00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:44.200
Your mission: decide whether the
large pizza is worth the money.
